<title>FRANCE: Detroyat cuts rating on Esso, stock falls.</title>
<headline>Detroyat cuts rating on Esso, stock falls.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment research consultancy Detroyat Associes lowered its rating on Esso, the French subsidiary of U.S. energy group Exxon, to sell from speculative buy without specifying a reason.</p>
<p>Esso on Friday announced a cut in its interim dividend to eight francs for 1996 from 17 francs for 1995, citing the negative impact on its refining results of insufficient stocks.</p>
<p>The board will set the 1996 dividend at a meeting scheduled for March 19. The gross dividend in 1995 was 25 francs.</p>
<p>Esso shares were down 6.38 percent at 646 francs at 1350 GMT on the Paris bourse.</p>
